From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bo-Cun Chen <bc-bocun.chen@mediatek.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 20:45:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: pcs: mtk-lynxi: fix link-flapping
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Fix the SGMII link flap issue.

This bad analog calibration situation only occurs on the MT7988 USXGMII,
and even if a MT7988 SGMII link‑down event happens, it will be recovered
automatically by the link_poll delayed‑work mechanism.

(cherry picked from commit e57f45d866f56031a1dabb4ae78c9070a4cca68a)
---
 drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c | 5 -----
 1 file changed, 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
index 7f788ea0fa82b..049e9f0afe63f 100644
--- a/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/pcs/pcs-mtk-lynxi.c
@@ -276,11 +276,6 @@ static void mtk_pcs_lynxi_link_up(struct phylink_pcs *pcs,
 	struct mtk_pcs_lynxi *mpcs = pcs_to_mtk_pcs_lynxi(pcs);
 	unsigned int sgm_mode;
 
-	if (mpcs->xfi_tphy) {
-		phy_reset(mpcs->xfi_tphy);
-		phy_set_mode_ext(mpcs->xfi_tphy, PHY_MODE_ETHERNET, interface);
-	}
-
 	if (neg_mode != PHYLINK_PCS_NEG_INBAND_ENABLED) {
 		/* Force the speed and duplex setting */
 		if (speed == SPEED_10)
